Title: Chapter 4: What the Viking Poets Knew
Output-Formats:
Last-Modified: 2026-08-16
Tagline: Poetry as error-correcting code. Kennings, rhyme, alliteration, meter, each a tool in the error-correction toolkit; metaphor is king of them all. Structure is a generator, a skaldic poem is a fractal encoding built the way a shipwright built a hull, and rules stay dead without the worked examples that carry the wisdom.
